{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/216497-what-changeling-would-you-be","id":216497,"title":"What Changeling Would You Be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-01T22:49:34-07:00","id":216497,"title":"What Changeling Would You Be?","content":"So a while ago, I made a thread asking which Kith you would be. This thread is a little different. It's used to explain which Seeming you would be from Ogre, Beast, Wizened, Elemental, Fairest, and Darkling. As well as listing which Court you'd be a member of and what you might offer the Court. Basically, if you were a Changeling, how would you fit into their society?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Here's mine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b> Beast<br /> <br /> Reasons: Although I wanted to say Ogre on this, I'm one of those people who prefers to suppress their anger until it explodes years later, rather than lash out all the time, and I'm not exactly strong enough for heavy duty activity. However, I associate more easily with animals than I do with people. Cats in particular, and I feel that if I were to be made a Changeling, then becoming one of the Beasts would be appropriate for that. I suppose if I can't have super strength, I'll have to make do with razor sharp claws, fangs, and heightened senses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Court:</b> Autumn<br /> <br /> Reasons: Fight fire with fire, as they say; and considering the towering inferno on the other side of The Hedge, I'm going to need a lot of fire if I plan to survive in the Freeholds. This was a very tough choice between Spring and Autumn. I'm a hedonist, I like to eat, sleep, play games, and generally slack off as opposed to doing too much work. Spring Court would probably have been perfect for me. However, I feel that if I discovered magic was real, I would jump on the chance to study it in further detail. I'm a fan of mythology, and it would probably be one of the few things to get me really motivated to get up and do some work. A life of indulgence is fun and all, but probably not as much fun as throwing fire balls or flinging cars around! A Court who is dedicated to the acquisition and practice of Fae magic would be more appealing to me, though that wouldn't stop me from paying a visit to Spring territory when I'm feeling a little stressed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Occupation:</b> Occultist, Researcher<br /> <br /> <br /> Reasons: Okay, so the supernatural is real; time to sort out fact from fiction before I go rushing off into a life and death battle! Don't want to pull out a crucifix just to see the local vampire snap it like a twig! Much like my choice for the Autumn Court, I'd want to study as much about the supernatural as I could. Finding out what is real and what is just fairy tales, as well as researching the various forms of magic at my disposal. Occultist is probably a more human term for Fae Scientist, as I'd probably have to use live test subjects to further explore the myths and facts the supernatural creatures had to offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-02-2014, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T00:04:57-07:00","id":216546,"title":"","content":"Changelings don't choose their seemings. The Others pick one for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T10:34:12-07:00","id":216799,"title":"","content":"1)True, but they have to work with what they get, so you characteristics can lead towards certain seemings over others.<br /> 2)Irony of me saying it, but let's not kill the fun before it starts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T12:41:10-07:00","id":216822,"title":"","content":"SEEMING: Wizened or Darkling- I'm pretty terrible socially, so I'm not a Fairest, not strong enough to be an Ogre, and too intellectual to fit as a Beast. I might end up a Elemental, but I'm not sure I'm that asocial. The presenceless Wizened and lone Darklings seem to fit. <br /> <br /> COURT: Autumn or Summer- Winter is right out; Their write-up in core makes them seem like cowards, and their entry in Lords of Summer makes them seem like jerks. Spring is a bit hedonistic for my prudish self. Autumn is the &quot;Smart guy&quot; group, which appeals to me, but their focus on fear can be a bit unhealthy. Summer, while a bit more martial than my usual inclinations, seems rather natural. After all, if you were kidnapped and had everything stolen from you, wouldn't you get furious? <br /> <br /> OCCUPATION: Researcher/scholar- No matter the Court, I'm a thinker, not a fighter. My studies would probably be more narrow(re:how to kill that thing) than in Autumn, but I think I can contribute either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T12:57:05-07:00","id":225238,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling that my background: outdoorsy (backpacking, hiking, etc), lover of whiskey, educator, and friend of dogs/cats would draw a keeper that would use me to either run errands between mountains, and possibly turn me into a beast. So broadback or maybe runnerswift? Essentially mountain goat-ish for carrying crap up and down trails. *Sigh* I can picture it now, the keeper picking up crap and buying things, and then shoving them into my pack, because he doesn't feel like carrying it, while I try to explain to him that he is standing in poison ivy, lol. When I get out I think I would be drawn to the spring court and just party, romping around in nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}